  "manual_review_reasoning": {
    "overall": "Coordinator read all six implementation spans and independently compared behavior, side effects, call chain and limitations against the authored receipts. Promotion records quality of these individual analyses only; it is not a finding disposition or workflow-completion claim.",
    "shift-close-preview": "PrepareShiftCloseHandler reads an Open shift AsNoTracking, computes expected cash via ShiftReconciliation, reads threshold, reconstructs Open Shift and returns discrepancy/approval calculation. No write/token. CloseShift path recomputes at execution; preview staleness alone is not a financial defect.",
    "employee-create": "CreateEmployee validates identity and parsable compensation enum and authorizes employees_manage, then stores raw compensation type and supplied signed amounts; no numeric sign/range guard. Deterministic request key/replay limits duplicate create. This supports an admission boundary concern but not unauthorized actor or realized payroll loss.",
    "attendance-check-in": "BiometricCheckIn uses Cairo business date and UTC time text; only same-date open shift establishes lateness. Daily wage movement key includes employee/date/shift and late penalty is guarded by positive wage; both are staged before one SaveChanges. Event ID is stored but deterministic ledger IDs provide the visible dedup boundary.",
    "employee-update": "UpdateEmployee authorizes and replaces compensation/profile fields without numeric amount guard or concurrency token; entity SaveChanges is last-writer-wins in source. No live concurrent overwrite was tested and UserId is not changed.",
    "attendance-check-out": "BiometricCheckOut reconstructs check-in timestamp using current UTC date plus stored HH:mm, computes/clamps worked minutes, overwrites attendance and posts positive overtime using employee/date key. Cross-UTC-midnight undercount is source-supported; repeat checkout can change recorded hours without changing already-existing deterministic movement. No realized underpayment is proven.",
    "daily-statement": "GetAsync sequentially composes independent read queries; selected-day flows and current treasury balances coexist, with no common snapshot transaction. This supports cross-section observation-time limitation; current balances are not falsely represented as historical. Multiple BusinessDay rows per date remains contingent on schema/policy."
